om/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "As discussed with @julianoes yesterday, while running Mission integration tests, I got below error:\n```\nWARN  [navigator] First waypoint too far away: 7094 meters, 900 max.\n```\nI'd set PX4 SITL Home to match First waypoint of Mission Survey as per @julianoes suggestion; I was able to run [MissionSurvey](https://github.com/dronecore/DroneCore/blob/develop/integration_tests/mission_survey.cpp#L50) test successfully.\nBut when I ran [MissionAddWaypointsAndFly](https://github.com/dronecore/DroneCore/blob/f0926830fd62b94d97609bf1bfbf31292acd2b2f/integration_tests/mission.cpp#L33), I got same error \n\nThis is because the First waypoint choosen for these two tests are far away from their relative PX4 SITL Home.\nSo, I recommend we have to choose First waypoint within 900 meters from default PX4 SITL Home so that we can run all Mission integration tests without a need to configure PX4 SITL Home.", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}"